I am pretty sure that Andy's installation notes can be relied upon, but for
the record here they are:
--------------------------README.INSTALL---------------------------------
Contained below this level is a UAE application area showing how
to add the 'motor' record to your system.

To install the 'motor' record into your EPICS release, please follow
the instructions given here:

***NOTE*** 
In "src", the original drvOms.[ch] have been renamed to drvSmOms6Axis.[ch]
so that both old and new versions of the steppermotor driver are
available. The "steppermotor" record talks to the old driver, the
"motor" record talks to the new driver.
***

(1) cp motor/src/drv* $EPICS/base/src/drv/old
(2) Edit $EPICS/base/src/drv/old/Makefile.Vx and add the line:
	SRCS.c += ../drvOms58.c
(3) Edit $EPICS/base/src/drv/combine/Makefile.Vx and add the line:
	LIBOBJS += $(DIR_OLD)/drvOms58.o
(4) cp motor/src/dev* $EPICS/base/src/dev
(5) Edit $EPICS/base/src/dev/Makefile.Vx and add the lines:
	SRCS.c += ../devOms.c
	SRCS.c += ../devOms58.c
(6) cp motor/src/recMotor.c $EPICS/base/src/rec
(7) Edit $EPICS/base/src/rec/Makefile.Vx and add the line:
	SRCS.c += ../recMotor.c
(8) cp motor/src/motor.h $EPICS/base/include
(9) cp motor/src/choiceMotor.h $EPICS/base/include
(10) cp motor/ascii/cat_ascii/motorRecord.ascii $EPICS/base/src/ascii
(11) Edit $EPICS/base/src/ascii/choiceRec.ascii and add the contents
     of motor/ascii/cat_ascii/choiceRec.ascii to it.
(12) Edit $EPICS/base/src/ascii/dbRecType.ascii and add the line:
	"motor"
(13) Edit $EPICS/base/src/ascii/devSup.ascii and add the lines:
	!Motor
	"motor"         VME_IO          "devOms"                "OMS VME8/44"
	"motor"         VME_IO          "devOms58"              "OMS VME58"
(14) Edit $EPICS/base/src/ascii/drvSup.ascii and add the line:
	"drvOms58"
(15) cp motor/capfast/*.sym $EPICS/extensions/src/edif/lib/sym
(16) cp motor/capfast/edb.def $EPICS/extensions/src/edif/lib/sym
(17) For version 2.2 of Capfast, edit $EPICS/extensions/src/edif/lib/epics*.mnu 
     to add the "motor" record.
     For version 3.02.xx of Capfast, edit $EPICS/extensions/src/edif/lib/menus.new/epics*.mnu 
     to add the "motor" record.

